This folder contains both the CLI version of the Speedtest.net website tool as well as an automated script
to test bandwidth at a site and record on the display in a powershell window as well as into 
the "TPT - Exchange to O365 Mail Migration Planning Document.xlsx" file on the Bandwidth tab (if  you put that file into c:\temp before you run this). 

speedtestPS.ps1:

1) make C:\temp if it doesn't exist
2) Check if Speedtest.exe is in the temp folder if not download it
3) Get a list of speedtest servers
4) Get the top two server's IDs
5) Run a speed test with the first server and record it
6) Run a speed test with the second server and record it
7) Calculate the average of the two tests and record it.
8) Export the speed test to a csv file with headers and line titles
9) Import the CSV into the "TPT - Exchange to O365 Mail Migration Planning Document.xlsx" file on the Bandwidth tab
10) Clean up downloaded and created files and imported PS modules. 





